=== Testing Capacity vs Orders Relationship ===
Finding minimum capacity needed for different order counts...

Full matching (1 price):
  Capacity: 10000, Orders attempted: 200000
  Placed: 200000, Rejected: 0
  Filled: 200000, Final open: 0
  Peak concurrent open: 0
  Efficiency: 100.0% placed
  Utilization: placed/capacity = 20.0x

Partial matching (10 prices):
  Capacity: 10000, Orders attempted: 200000
  Placed: 11112, Rejected: 188888
  Filled: 1112, Final open: 10000
  Peak concurrent open: 10000
  Efficiency: 5.6% placed
  Utilization: placed/capacity = 1.1x

Wide spread (100 prices):
  Capacity: 10000, Orders attempted: 200000
  Placed: 10102, Rejected: 189898
  Filled: 102, Final open: 10000
  Peak concurrent open: 10000
  Efficiency: 5.1% placed
  Utilization: placed/capacity = 1.0x

Very wide (1000 prices):
  Capacity: 10000, Orders attempted: 200000
  Placed: 10012, Rejected: 189988
  Filled: 12, Final open: 10000
  Peak concurrent open: 10000
  Efficiency: 5.0% placed
  Utilization: placed/capacity = 1.0x

=== Key Insight ===
Minimum capacity needed = peak concurrent open orders
If orders match immediately (same price), capacity can be tiny.
If orders don't match (spread prices), capacity must hold all open.
